# Cache + security headers.
#
# ⚠ AS OF THIS WRITING THIS FILE IS NOT IN EFFECT. onemorebng.org is served by a
# Cloudflare Worker whose config lives outside this repo, and it applies its own
# blanket "max-age=0, must-revalidate" to everything. Verified against the live
# site: even main.js comes back must-revalidate, not the immutable set below.
#
# The same goes for vercel.json and netlify.toml. All three are kept in sync and
# accurate so that they're correct if the site ever moves hosts (Cloudflare
# Pages and Netlify read this file; Vercel reads vercel.json) — but today the
# Worker decides. Change caching there, not here.
#
# The rule that matters wherever it's applied: data.js and sanity-config.js must
# NEVER be cached as immutable. They are content, not code — caching them for a
# year means owner edits never reach anyone who has visited before.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/assets/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/video/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/js/main.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/js/data.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/js/sanity-config.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
